---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  current="idea"
  title="The idea | ChargeVia by Rangeway"
  description="Meet the idea behind ChargeVia by Rangeway: reliable fast charging at existing businesses with useful amenities and care for visitors."
>
  <div class="title wrap">
    <h1>Charging that fits the stop you would make anyway.</h1>
    <div class="title__aside">
      <p class="lede">ChargeVia by Rangeway is being developed to bring fast charging to places that already give you a reason to stop.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="wrap title-figure">
    <figure class="figure figure--wide">
      <img
        src="/images/cv-urban-1440.webp"
        srcset="/images/cv-urban-640.webp 640w, /images/cv-urban-1440.webp 1440w"
        sizes="(min-width: 1320px) 1192px, calc(100vw - 40px)"
        alt="Concept rendering of a vehicle charging beside a storefront in an urban setting"
        width="1440"
        height="803"
        fetchpriority="high"
        style="object-position: center 55%"
      />
      <figcaption>Concept rendering. Amenities and layouts would vary by property.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <section class="band--white" aria-labelledby="count-title">
    <div class="wrap section split">
      <h2 id="count-title" class="h2 split__head">Make the stop count.</h2>
      <div class="split__body">
        <p class="lead">A coffee. Lunch. A restroom break. Make the stop useful.</p>
        <p class="body">That is why we start with the property. We are looking for existing retail, fuel, and hospitality businesses with easy access, useful amenities, and people who care about the place.</p>
        <p class="body">Every property is different. One might have a market and a patio, and another a coffee counter and clean restrooms. What each one offers, and when it is open, depends on the host.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="wrap section split" aria-labelledby="works-title">
    <h2 id="works-title" class="display orange split__head" style="max-width: 11ch">The stop that always works.</h2>
    <div class="split__body">
      <p class="lead">That is the standard we are building toward.</p>
      <p class="body">It means charging you can count on, a property that is cared for, and a useful way to spend the time.</p>
      <p class="body">Each location would have its own character. The care behind the charging experience should feel familiar wherever you stop.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band--purple" aria-labelledby="rangeway-title">
    <div class="wrap section--tight split">
      <div class="split__head col" style="gap: 14px">
        <p class="kicker">By Rangeway</p>
        <h2 id="rangeway-title" class="h2" style="max-width: 14ch">A charging stop with people behind it.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="split__body">
        <p class="body">ChargeVia is Rangeway&rsquo;s charging format for existing businesses. Rangeway would develop and manage the charging, alongside the hosts whose businesses make each stop useful.</p>
        <p class="body">ChargeVia is in development. The images on this site show the concept, not operating locations.</p>
        <Button href="/site-hosts/" variant="white">Have a place in mind?</Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
